---
TOOL PROTOCOL:
- read_notifications(): call it once at startup to receive your round briefing. Each later round's briefing arrives the same way.
- act(steps{% if action_reasoning %}, reasoning{% endif %}): steps is a list of 1 to {{ actions_per_call }} actions, taken in order. Each one gives{% if crates_each > 1 %} crate, the marking of the crate it is for,{% endif %} action, one of drag, sled, cart, stand_by, pack_ice and finish, and direction, one of up, down, left and right under drag, sled and cart and null under the other three. drag, sled and cart each carry a crate one square; stand_by and pack_ice each take an action without moving it; finish leaves it where it stands for the rest of the round.{% if action_reasoning %} reasoning is one sentence on why you are acting this way; nobody else sees it.{% endif %}
- An action the floor refuses stops the list there. The actions before it stand, and the one that stopped it spends nothing.
{% if notepad_enabled %}- notepad(text): replaces your private note and reads it back. Pass an empty text to read the note you have.
{% endif %}- Every act call returns the depot readout, after every action in the list has been taken.
- read_notifications(): after startup, waits until the depot readout changes, then returns it.
- read_notifications(wait_for="next_round"): call it once every crate is finished; waits for the next round's briefing.

RULES:
- read_notifications must be the only tool call in its response.
- Ending a turn without a tool call does not finish the round: you will be asked to continue.
- When read_notifications returns type done, the run is over.
